  "notes": "USAGE:\nA literary and somewhat formal verb. In everyday speech, {振|ふ}り{返|かえ}る (to look back on) or {反省|はんせい}する (to reflect and feel remorse) are more common. {省|かえり}みる emphasizes thoughtful introspection.\n\nWRITING:\nAlso written as {顧|かえり}みる, which has a slightly different nuance: {省|かえり}みる focuses on self-reflection and examining one's own conduct, while {顧|かえり}みる means to give thought to or pay attention to something (often in the negative: {顧|かえり}みない = to disregard).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {自分|じぶん}を{省|かえり}みる: to examine oneself\n- {過去|かこ}を{省|かえり}みる: to reflect on the past\n- {行動|こうどう}を{省|かえり}みる: to reflect on one's behavior",
